Kinetic fling: correct the velocity estimate and bound stacked-flick accumulation.

Three device-measured corrections to the touch fling, all in the kinetic velocity
estimator, each env-gated so it can be A/B'd without a rebuild.

1. Velocity is measured across the motion samples only. A gesture's terminal event
   carries a zero delta; including its timestamp in the (last - first) span would
   stretch the denominator and under-report the fling. appendToScrollHistory() also
   no longer lets a zero-delta end event prune the motion samples that define the
   velocity, and never lets such events accumulate. WEBKIT_KINETIC_END_EVENT_FIX=0
   restores upstream.

2. The N/(N-1) inflation is removed. N samples contribute N deltas but (last - first)
   spans only the N-1 intervals between them, so every fling was over-fast by a
   device-measured 1.09-1.12x. Each delta is now charged one mean interval, making
   the estimate sample-count independent. WEBKIT_KINETIC_VELOCITY_BIAS_FIX=0 restores
   the upstream arithmetic.

3. Stacked-flick accumulation is bounded. accumulateVelocity() adds a multiple of the
   previous fling's velocity for a same-direction flick and feeds the sum forward;
   upstream caps the multiplier at 6, so feed-scrolling (YouTube) compounds into a
   runaway far faster than the finger asked. The multiplier cap now defaults to 1.0
   and the accumulated result is clamped absolutely. WEBKIT_KINETIC_VELOCITY_ACCUM_MAX
   (0..6, 6 = upstream) and WEBKIT_KINETIC_MAX_VELOCITY (px/s, 0 = no clamp) tune both.

Must apply AFTER webkit-kinetic-decel-friction-env.patch and
webkit-kinetic-jank-resilient-end.patch (same file).

